    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-18T04:10:01+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-18T04:10:01+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-17T18:40:01Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-17T18:40:01Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A strong high pressure system centred over Victoria will maintain a ridge across SA as it drifts slowly over NSW. A cold front will then approach from the west late Saturday and move across SA on Sunday, before another ridge pushes in behind the front. The associated high will then move eastwards across waters south from Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW015" description="Mount Lofty Ranges" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light in the late afternoon then becoming north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 19 and 22.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light in the late afternoon then becoming northerly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. Slight chance of a shower in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northwesterly 30 to 45 km/h turning west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 13 and 16.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
